 ## Overview
-DAVIGS is a plug-and-play appearance modeling method for Gaussian Splatting that mitigates appearance variation-induced floaters and color distortions by transforming rendered images at the image level using 3D consistent features [S1]. It decouples global view-dependent appearance variations (e.g., daylight, ISPs) from local spatial changes (e.g., street lamps) without compromising rendering speed [S1]. Unlike coupled methods that manipulate Gaussian properties and slow rendering, DAVIGS transforms results at the image level, allowing the appearance module to be discarded after optimization [S1].
+DAVIGS is a plug-and-play appearance modeling method for Gaussian Splatting that decouples global view-dependent appearance variations (e.g., daylight, ISPs) from local spatial changes (e.g., street lamps) by transforming rendered images at the image level using 3D consistent features [S1]. It mitigates appearance variation-induced floaters and color distortions without compromising rendering speed, distinguishing itself from coupled methods that manipulate Gaussian properties and from simple decoupled methods that lack 3D consistency [S1].
 
